Package: poisECM
Title: Poisson generalized spatial linear model for analyzing multi-sample count data
Version: 0.1
Authors@R: 
    person("Florica", "Constantine", email = "florica@berkeley.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Maintainer: Florica Constantine <florica@berkeley.edu>
Description:  Fit a Poisson generalized spatial linear model for analyzing 
  multi-sample count data. This model allows for disconnected samples with 
  different coordinate systems that do not necessarily align, all while 
  estimating of a common set of fixed effects across samples. 
  E.g., consider a dataset with tissue samples from multiple patients from 
  different conditions---this model will enable estimating fixed effects for 
  conditions while accounting for the heterogeneity in spatial correlation 
  structures across tissue samples. 
